Implement parameterized queries even in test fixtures to establish secure patterns:
```javascript
async query(sql, params = []) {
  if (typeof sql !== 'string' || !Array.isArray(params)) {
    throw new Error('Invalid query parameters');
  }
  console.log('[sql]', sql, '[params]', params);
  return [];
}
```

Add a redaction mechanism or use proper logging levels:
```javascript
const sanitizedSql = sql.replace(/password\s*=\s*'[^']*'/gi, "password='***'");
console.log('[sql]', sanitizedSql);
```
Or better: use environment-aware logging that doesn't run in production.

Add basic error simulation capability:
```javascript
async query(sql, params = []) {
  console.log('[sql]', sql);
  if (sql.includes('INVALID')) {
    throw new Error('Query failed');
  }
  return [];
}
```
This helps test error paths in consuming code.

Make the fixture configurable:
```javascript
export async function createConnection(mockResults = {}) {
  return {
    async query(sql) {
      console.log('[sql]', sql);
      return mockResults[sql] || [];
    }
  };
}
```

Add minimal lifecycle methods:
```javascript
export async function createConnection() {
  return {
    async query(sql) {
      console.log('[sql]', sql);
      return [];
    },
    async close() {
      console.log('[db] Connection closed');
    },
    async beginTransaction() {},
    async commit() {},
    async rollback() {}
  };
}
```

